# HMS Module Catalog (source-controlled defaults)

Product module names and responsibilities align with [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../app-write-up.mdc). This file is the entitlement catalog: each entry declares a stable `module_key`, default permissions (from [permissions.mdc](./permissions.mdc)), and which subscription packages include it (see [subscriptions.mdc](./subscriptions.mdc)).

## Rules

- This file is the complete source-controlled catalog of shipped active modules; setup must seed it out of the box.
- Every module **must** declare default permissions using the vocabulary in `permissions.mdc`.
- Users may be assigned multiple modules; effective access is always intersected with the active subscription package.
- Authorized administrators may customize, extend, or reset module permissions to shipped defaults; every change is atomic, versioned, and auditable.
- Reset must restore the shipped module-permission mapping completely. Failure rolls back without leaving partial or excess access.
- Planned modules (`status: planned`) are documented but excluded from default seed until implemented.
- Frontend menus, routes, and actions for a module must not appear unless the module is in the user's effective set.

